{
  "_id": "tg-eye",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "eat thereof, then your eyes shall be opened, Gen. 3:5 (Moses 4:11). Eye for eye, Ex. 21:24 (Lev. 24:20; Deut. 19:21; Matt. 5:38; 3 Ne. 12:38). every man whatsoever is right in his own eyes, Deut. 12:8. the apple of his eye, Deut. 32:10 (Ps. 17:8). Philistines took him, and put out his eyes, Judg. 16:21. that which was right in his own eyes, Judg. 17:6 (21:25). Lord opened the eyes of the young man, 2 Kgs. 6:17. eyes shall not see all the evil, 2 Kgs. 22:20 (2 Chr. 34:28). put out the eyes of Zedekiah, 2 Kgs. 25:7 (Jer. 39:7; 52:11). eyes of the Lord run to and fro, 2 Chr. 16:9. commandment of the Lord is pure, enlightening the eyes, Ps. 19:8. Mine eyes are ever toward the Lord, Ps. 25:15. eye of the Lord is upon them that fear him, Ps. 33:18. eyes of the Lord are upon the righteous, Ps. 34:15 (1 Pet. 3:12). light of mine eyes … is gone from me, Ps. 38:10. he that formed the eye, shall he not see, Ps. 94:9. eyes have they, but they see not, Ps. 115:5 (135:16). Be not wise in thine own eyes, Prov. 3:7. ways of man are before the eyes of the Lord, Prov. 5:21. way of a fool is right in his own eyes, Prov. 12:15. eyes of the Lord are in every place, Prov. 15:3. ways of a man are clean in his own eyes, Prov. 16:2. a generation that are pure in their own eyes, Prov. 30:12. wise man’s eyes are in his head, Eccl. 2:14. Woe unto them that are wise in their own eyes, Isa. 5:21 (2 Ne. 15:21). shut their eyes, Isa. 6:10 (Matt. 13:15; John 12:40; Acts 28:27; 2 Ne. 16:10). sleep, and hath closed your eyes, Isa. 29:10 (Rom. 11:8; 2 Ne. 27:5). eyes of the blind shall be opened, Isa. 35:5. they shall see eye to eye, Isa. 52:8. neither hath the eye seen … what he hath prepared, Isa. 64:4 (1 Cor. 2:9; D&C 76:10). which have eyes, and see not, Jer. 5:21 (Ezek. 12:2). eyes of the Lord God are upon the sinful, Amos 9:8.",
